    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a written prevention plan given. Depression, anxiety, alcohol, drug use, tobacco, and personal-safety screens are negative. Blood pressure 108/68 mmHg is normal. [S]<list><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Post-infectious ME/CFS, moderate and improving (G93.32)</content>. Stable on her energy management plan, with no crash since the July flare. [S]<list><item>Continue the care and support plan; next ME/CFS review in about three months.</item><item>Today&apos;s vaccine was scheduled with a rest day after it, as she prefers.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Vitamin D deficiency, replete (E55.9)</content>. 25-hydroxyvitamin D 34 ng/mL at last month&apos;s review. [S]<list><item>Continue cholecalciferol 2,000 units daily.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cervical cancer screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Normal HPV and cytology co-test about four years ago; next due in about one year</td></tr><tr><td>Breast cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Mammography every two years starts at 40. No family history of breast or ovarian cancer is recorded</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 score 4, with item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Anxiety screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>GAD-7 score 3</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 1</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy drug use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No drug use</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Never smoker</td></tr><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>108/68 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time antigen and antibody test, with her consent; suggested at the infectious diseases consultation</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time antibody test with reflex RNA, with her consent</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time triple panel (surface antigen, surface antibody, and core antibody); she completed a vaccine series years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Intimate partner violence screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Asked privately with a brief screening tool; negative</td></tr><tr><td>Pregnancy intention and contraception</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Not planning a pregnancy; satisfied with her copper intrauterine device</td></tr><tr><td>Folic acid</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Counseled that anyone who could become pregnant should take 0.4 to 0.8 mg of folic acid daily</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>This season&apos;s vaccine given today</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended; she will book it at her pharmacy two weeks from now, with a rest day planned after it</td></tr><tr><td>Tdap</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Given about five years ago; next booster due in about five years</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Adult three-dose series completed years ago for her nursing work</td></tr><tr><td>HPV vaccine</td><td>Declined</td><td>Shared decision for adults 27 to 45; after discussion she declined</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes and cholesterol screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Diabetes screening is for adults 35 to 70 with overweight or obesity, and her BMI is 19.4; HbA1c was 5.1% at intake. Statin assessment starts at 40</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Starts at 45</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, 2026-2027 season [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: HIV, hepatitis C, and hepatitis B results will be sent when available. COVID-19 vaccine at her pharmacy. ME/CFS review in about three months. Next preventive visit in one year. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
